From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:17:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] emit-rtl: Do not access BB_END/BB_HEAD of non-BB_RTL blocks
 [PR125582]

Since r16-1398, expanded blocks stay non-BB_RTL until the end of
expansion, but BLOCK_FOR_INSN of their insns is already set.
mips16_gp_pseudo_reg emits the $gp load after the basic block note of
such a block, and add_insn_after then crashes on BB_END.  Only touch
BB_END and BB_HEAD of BB_RTL blocks; pass_expand::execute sets them
for the others from head_end_for_bb.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5

	PR target/125582

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* emit-rtl.cc (add_insn_after): Only update BB_END for BB_RTL
	blocks.
	(add_insn_before): Only check BB_HEAD for BB_RTL blocks.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/mips/pr125582.c: New test.

Link: https://inbox.sourceware.org/gcc-patches/20261007211753.3755573-1-julius@bairaktaris.de/
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
 gcc/emit-rtl.cc                          |  9 ++++++---
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/mips/pr125582.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/mips/pr125582.c

--- a/gcc/emit-rtl.cc
+++ b/gcc/emit-rtl.cc
@@ -4368,8 +4368,10 @@ add_insn_after (rtx_insn *insn, rtx_insn
       if (INSN_P (insn))
 	df_insn_rescan (insn);
       /* Should not happen as first in the BB is always
-	 either NOTE or LABEL.  */
-      if (BB_END (bb) == after
+	 either NOTE or LABEL.  Blocks expanded but not yet BB_RTL
+	 have no BB_END.  */
+      if ((bb->flags & BB_RTL)
+	  && BB_END (bb) == after
 	  /* Avoid clobbering of structure when creating new BB.  */
 	  && !BARRIER_P (insn)
 	  && !NOTE_INSN_BASIC_BLOCK_P (insn))
@@ -4403,7 +4405,8 @@ add_insn_before (rtx_insn *insn, rtx_ins
 	df_insn_rescan (insn);
       /* Should not happen as first in the BB is always either NOTE or
 	 LABEL.  */
-      gcc_assert (BB_HEAD (bb) != insn
+      gcc_assert (!(bb->flags & BB_RTL)
+		  || BB_HEAD (bb) != insn
 		  /* Avoid clobbering of structure when creating new BB.  */
 		  || BARRIER_P (insn)
 		  || NOTE_INSN_BASIC_BLOCK_P (insn));
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/mips/pr125582.c
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+/* PR target/125582 */
+/* { dg-do compile } */
+/* { dg-options "-mabicalls -fpic -mips16" } */
+
+int foo (void *, unsigned, unsigned);
+
+static int
+bar (int *p)
+{
+  int ret;
+
+  do
+    ret = foo (p, sizeof (*p), 1);
+  while (ret == -1);
+
+  return ret;
+}
+
+int
+baz (void)
+{
+  int x = 1;
+
+  return bar (&x);
+}
